{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q2584366","formula":"XeOF₄","hill":"F4OXe","elements":["O","F","Xe"],"composition":{"F":4.0,"O":1.0,"Xe":1.0},"names":{"en":"Xenon oxytetrafluoride","ru":"Оксид-тетрафторид ксенона"},"descriptions":{"en":"Xenon oxytetrafluoride (XeOF4) is an inorganic chemical compound. It is an unstable colorless liquid with a melting point of −46.2 °C (−51.2 °F; 227.0 K) that can be synthesized by partial hydrolysis of XeF6, or the reaction of XeF6 with silica or NaNO3: NaNO3 + XeF6 → NaF + XeOF4 + FNO2 A high-yield synthesis proceeds by the reaction of XeF6 with POF3 at −196 °C (−320.8 °F; 77.1 K). Like most xenon oxides, it is extremely reactive, and it hydrolyses in water to give hazardous and corrosive products, including hydrogen fluoride: 2 XeOF4 + 4 H2O → 2 Xe + 8 HF + 3 O2 In addition, some ozone and fluorine is formed.","ru":"Окси́д-тетрафтори́д ксено́на(VI) (оксотетрафтори́д ксено́на), XeOF4 — неорганическое соединение ксенона с кислородом и фтором. Бесцветная жидкость. Растворим в безводном HF. Гидролизуется с образованием XeO2F2 и ХеО3."},"fame":19,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":"O=[Xe](F)(F)(F)F","inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":null,"atoms":6,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.075,"y":-1.157,"z":0.123,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.026,"y":0.306,"z":-0.725,"el":"Xe"},{"x":1.915,"y":1.077,"z":-0.587,"el":"F"},{"x":-1.754,"y":-0.797,"z":-0.022,"el":"F"},{"x":1.16,"y":-1.073,"z":-0.186,"el":"F"},{"x":-1.37,"y":1.644,"z":0.036,"el":"F"}],"bonds":[[0,1,2.0],[1,2,1.0],[1,3,1.0],[1,4,1.0],[1,5,1.0]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2584366","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://